scpp -- the selective C preprocessor====================================    scpp -MWIDTH prog.c    scpp -M"MAXINT MININT" -DDEBUG=0 prog.c > out.cscpp copies C source to standard output and expands ONLY the macros youname, leaving every other #define, #include and macro use exactly as itwas.  It is for clearing conditional code or one misleading macro out of afile without running the whole preprocessor over it.  -Mname   interpret this macro (or a quoted list of names)  -Dname   define it -- as 1, or as -Dname=value -- which implies -M  -C       keep comments inside the macro definitions it interprets  -Idir    add a directory to search for #include filesWith no file it reads standard input; `-' names standard input too.By Brad Needham, Tektronix, Inc.  This is TOP release 2's OS-9 build; itssource and manual are in SRC/scpp.